{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/28126-the-heat-is-on-ic-game-thread","id":28126,"title":"The Heat is....ON! - IC Game Thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-11T11:21:33-08:00","id":28126,"title":"The Heat is....ON! - IC Game Thread","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1-mU-YSk32I\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1-mU-YSk32I\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1-mU-YSk32I </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1-mU-YSk32I\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1-mU-YSk32I </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This is the IC thread for the Demon PbP.<br /> <br /> Calrabjohns and Squidheadjax are the players and I am GM.<br /> <br /> One player is newly fallen (first scene in fact) and the other will be hunting them down trying to find out what's happening.<br /> <br /> To keep <i>some</i> semblance of mystery the players should be posting their individual bits and pieces in [spoiler] tags.<br /> <br /> Dice rolls can use invisible castle or just roll analog and tell me me he results.<br /> <br /> Let's do this!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T08:45:52-08:00","id":28748,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"left\">Tommy shrugged off his black leather jacket and stowed it in his locker with a neatly ironed white button-down shirt on the hanger, trading his spiffy duds for a loose fitting gray sweatshirt and atop that a bright thin cloth orange vest with reflectors studding the sleeves, front and back. He looked at the mirror stuck to the interior of the locker door with a sigh that didn't quite convey the bored, resigned tone he meant it to and moved with a rote sensibility as he:</div><ul><li>runs a pocket comb to slick back his black hair,</li> <li>puts the comb away,</li> <li>looks in the mirror for a second,</li> <li>dab with the tip of thumb and index finger at smoothing his eye-brows and pencilled looking mustache,</li> <li>engage in light ribalding with night manager Reginald Barnes</li> </ul><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">&quot;Is tonight the night your mail order bride finally gets here, Thomas?&quot;</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Tommy pushes the locker door shut and turns around, leans back and stares a moment at Mr. Barnes before a grin slides into place, &quot;Well we can't all be married to pastries, Reggie. It's not my fault I'm so damn pretty,&quot; finishing with a flourished pull on the hood and walking on the tiled floor toward the door with two steps forward and one to the right, or two forward one left in an L like a chess knight.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Reginald was about to say something to counter in his dry fashion when he caught the L steps out of the corner of his eye. He looked up from the clipboard he'd been reading, &quot;You're a bit touched, aren't you Thomas. Try not to break any of the cargo when you unload,&quot; curtly handing over the clipboard to Tommy.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">&quot;We're shorthanded tonight and it says in your file you're adequate at operating a lift. The containers from Taiwan need to be off-loaded. Client is unhappy, as if we can control the weather-- nevermind: are you able to do this without damaging our charges?&quot;</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Tommy turned around and tipped his hood forward a little like a hat, &quot;I'll be ya huckleberry Reg.&quot;</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Reginald would have said something when he noticed powder on his hands and blushed, instead flustered and gesturing at the door.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">The night air felt pleasantly cool and the weather would have been perfect but for a fog blanketing the pier. Tommy looked around for a moment before feeling secure enough to let lenses slide down from beneath his eye lids and a tug at his ear lobes to trigger mechanisms for filtering ambient noise and environmental conditions. He was greeted with mild irritation, &quot;<i><span style=\"color:gray\">Do you always have to take so long, Y***d? In any event, switch to another frequency and set to alternate every two minutes. With luck, we're done tonight.</span></i>&quot;</div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"color:gray\">Alright Unit Yesod. You have the manifest in hand- it's crate A2478S34281531-(city name)-UK. It's marked with a fluctuating UV stamp, the signature of the spectrum shifts fifteen seconds each interval. Your accompanying Gemurah partner will arrive the moment the package is en route. Acquisition and delivery is your mission. Do not deviate. Silence herein. Unit Binah signing off.</span></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Tommy/Yesod pushed the janitorial supplies ahead of him on the way to the forklift. Just because he was pulling the lift didn't stop his normal job from being next on the list. He hitched the cart to the lift and drove at half speed toward the east end of the dock. It wasn't often he could feel the air while between states so he made the most of it. After making sure Reginald or someone else wasn't passing by in the pier or within a half-mile on the block he undid the bolt and walked into the crate.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">As he verified the crate and pulled out the UV marked painting, he could feel vibrations in the air that translated to an incoming phone call which he rerouted to his ear and mouth directly rather than risk the phone as an intermediary to be tapped, the bits of data plucked from the waves and translated to caller ID. </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">&quot;Vin-nnny, the ninny, now why would you be calling me while I'm at the docks. You know that Mr. John Marzini doesn't appreciate---let's say initiative. I'm not on the clock with him right now.&quot;</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">&quot;Wow. Ya know, Tommy, it's funny you mention initiative because it looks to me like you seem to be indulging in that right now in that big old crate with the dinged up paint.&quot;</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> Tommy/Yesod carefully put down the painting and edged his way from the shipping container. He cast his sight around which earned him a derisive snort from the call. </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">&quot;The fuck are ya doing? Ah'm using a high powered set of binoculars with infrared, ultrared, shit the bed vision. And you definitely shit the bed.&quot;</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Undeterred by the invective, he continued to search for Vinny until an exasperated caller chimed in, &quot;You're supposed to be some genius forger and clean salesman but you can't wrap your head around a pair of binoculars. Fine. You want to know where I am? Seventh floor of the Thrifton building, southeast window. I'm next to some lady's desk. She's got those metal balls that bounce back and forward and back, a kitten on a tree and I'm givin you a two finger salute.&quot;</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;Unit Yesod, I'm picking up a hostile call and the package hasn't been sent. We're preparing an S-Gem to eliminate this interloper. Compromise can come at any time.&quot;</span></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Yesod scrambled his call with Vinny and patched into a frequency to Binah, &quot;Don't do that please...we're supposed to lock down this route for future deliveries. I can talk him down. Don't dispatch the S-Gem.&quot; He held his breath and waited. The answer came in the form of terminating the call and patch back to Vinny. He inwardly sighed in relief and tuned his voice back to heavy Brooklyn inflections then looked directly toward the southeast window.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">&quot;You finished being cute? You really think I would be out here and busting into a crate if I didn't know there was some primo art inside that I can unload at Samson or direct to Yuri. That maybe I've already got some chemically treated paints oxidized to appear 132 years old, ready to put to canvas so I can double down and deliver John his 80% after I've moved both? Did any of that occur to you? No it did not. Because you have some toy binoculars and wanted to bust my balls while unloading yours. Talk to him tomorrow and find out.&quot;</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">He could hear Vinny fuming on the other end, desperate to find a reason to look through a scope instead. Finally Vinny just hung up or he would have if Tommy/Yesod didn't keep the line open on a one way channel. He didn't want any other surprises from an enterprising, pissed off wise guy tonight.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">He went back into the crate and completed verification of the package: a blueprint with ink that scrambled into six different patterns that interchanged with varying frequency. After rolling it up carefully, he placed it into a pressurized tube that he then carefully put in a satchel on his shoulder.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">With that secure, he replaced the painting into its frame and turned it over hoping for something he might make good on. He was surprised to find a Goya staring him in the face. While he was glad to have something that could get him out of the Vinny jackpot, the painting that he now secreted away to the cart did not bode well.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> Putting it out of mind, Tommy/Yesod left the container and bolted it back up. &quot;This is Unit Yesod calling in. Bring out Unit Gemurah now. Something feels off. Nothing to do with the man on the phone. We should be out in five though.&quot;</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> The air crackled for a moment and like that there was a large man sitting in the carriage of a wrecking ball parked in the pier. He stretched his legs lazily on top of the console and looked down at Yesod with a glazed expression, &quot;Not like you to call early. We've done this I don't know how many times off-hand. Maybe that thug got under your skin. </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Yesod wanted to press the point but there wasn't time. His eyelids flickered as he ran through every subroutine programmed into this iteration and then his body seemed to peel away, scattering like strips that then joined back together and in that moment he was transformed. The satchel had melted away and the tube slotted into the left compartment of his true form: a hovering hour glass turned on its side.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">The tube burst apart and looked like millions of tiny dots. Ribbons of light moved back and forth, analyzing the blueprint for retention of the information while it prepped for transport. There was little that could conceal itself once Yesod took his true form and in that moment he saw two demons. He played the light pattern in a broken hybrid of Morse code and shorthand terms unique to Gemurah and himself to alert him of their company. All hell broke loose.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">One of them started to move toward Yesod with a curious expression on its face. Before it could break out, Gemurah shorn his skin and let loose a surge of electricity, causing the wrecking ball to start abruptly. It slammed into the moving demon and split it into two but not before Yesod saw that it had readied a charge to go on impact. He tapped into the phone line quickly as he heard Vinny wondering what the hell was happening, &quot;Get off the binoculars now!&quot;</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">The warning had come too late. A blinding plume of white light engulfed the pier, its effects like concentrated sunlight. There was a scream over the phone line and Yesod knew that Vinny hadn't turned away in time. If his optic nerves weren't fried completely and brain scrambled, he'd have to wear bifocals or something for the rest of his days at best.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">The second demon stationed by the container hatched out of his skin and swerved rapidly on his stomach through the burning light toward Gemurah. He seemed to be all limbs, wrapping itself around Gemurah and constricting the movement, squeezing Gemurah so tight that it would have snapped three bands of steel without pause.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Yesod kept trying to call in to Binah as it was evident to him that these demons did not care whether they made it back. &quot;I haven't finished the transition but the information is backed up. Let me stop this and assist Gemu...,&quot; <span style=\"color:gray\">&quot;This eventuality was not past our foresight and indeed we warned <b>you</b> of compromise. You are not to abandon your position. Secure the package. Gemurah will handle this and if not---there are others.&quot;</span></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Yesod disabled his autonomic defenses to free up processing speed but he wouldn't risk anything more in the pursuit to help Gemurah. The many tendriled demon began to leak acid from the end of each limb affixed to Gemurah. Yesod began to see beneath the chestplate of the behemoth to gears whirring. Gemurah dislodged his jaw and clamped down on the demon's head, a surge of power flowing through the gears, past his throat and lining each of Gemurah's teeth. &quot;We had a good run. See you soon.&quot; </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> The gears slowed and Gemurah focused everything to immolate himself and the other demon who tried to disengage. He held him fast and in the next instant a red light shot upward piercing through the white flare that was obfuscating everything in the pier. Yesod hadn't quite managed to pull up his defenses in time and the surge buffeted against him. Some of it he deferred into finishing the transport but the rest was burning him as he hovered there. </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"color:gray\">New parameters are to collect the cores and eyes of the aberrations and Gemurah. Afterwards, go into the shipping container where an extract will occur. There's too much risk to using you as an asset. </span></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Yesod used the cover of the corona to move about the pier and collect the cores along with eyes as directed. This mission seemed doomed from the get. And what was with the first demon---it barely did anything. These were the thoughts running through his head as he regarded the eyes on the ground. Confusion bloomed as he began to read an energy signature emanating from the eyes and that's when it happened.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">A flicker of recognition flashed in the disconnected eyes before coils shot out and wrapped about Yesod, breaking through the plating and transport chambers.He was dragged onto the stone masonry of the pier and being rewritten. Every function abandoned him and sound would not heed his call. The white and red light blanketing the pier dispersed in one last blaze.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">He dimly realized that he could see the stars now. The fog was gone, burned away. The shipping container looked like it had been smelted. He struggled to his feet and tried to nudge the bolt. There was no give. Scraps of metal were littered about the ground and somehow half of the cart, which he stood in front of to brace himself survived with miraculously the painting intact and now concealed by him.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">A whisper was registering inside his head that he knew could only be that demon who never lifted a finger. Reginald must have heard something because he was making his way down to see Tommy. Something was wrong with this whole mission: the Goya painting that held the blueprint was none other than &quot;All Will Fall.&quot; </div></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/257-calrabjohns","name":"Calrabjohns","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T16:51:38-08:00","id":29003,"title":"","content":"A pale brunette waits at the Indian restaurant next to the city park, thumbing with less-than-rapt interest through several activism-oriented Twitter feeds and Tumblrs on her slightly outdated iPhone. She suddenly goes perfectly still; even the gold-on-green fabric of the sari she wore for the occasion refuses to make the slightest flutter. Green eyes flash to the broad window showing the park and the night sky as her phone slips into her purse. She stands, letting a few pound notes tumble from her hand to the table to pay for her drink as she leaves. &quot;Give the councilor my apologies,&quot; she tells the proprietor as she slips a practical black fleece jacket on over her curve-flattering outfit. After slinking way through the light crowd coming in for dinner, the politically active heiress drops her indulgent expression and watches the sky blankly as she walks on in her low, gold-flecked heels.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Her flat is only one block down - &quot;Much more practical than a mostly-empty mansion,&quot; she always tells anyone who asks. It's certainly more practical than a mansion that doesn't really exist. She lets the indulgence of one relieved breath slip out as she closes the door behind her and pulls out the phone again. &quot;Edward, bring the car.&quot;<br /> <br /> A few minutes later, Stephanie Marks descends to the street again. Her wavy, dark hair has been pulled back in a ponytail and mostly covered by a black beret. Black turtleneck, black slacks, flat black shoes. A somewhat redundant black scarf drapes around her neck.<br /> &quot;Milady.&quot; Pushing nearly two meters in height, and not much less in width, the cultist in a black suit seems to make even the black luxury car he waits beside seem small. <br /> &quot;Not where people might hear, Edward,&quot; she grouses back at him, having resigned weeks ago to this little ritual. Oh well. It had been his lease she'd traded for to get her current flat, and his mostly-forgotten childhood friendship with one of the city councilors that had gotten her the meeting... she just skipped out of. Oh well. That and his service are worth a bit of mortal uppityness, even though he has been well-compensated.<br /> <br /> &quot;Where to?&quot; he asks once they're both in the car. &quot;Just drive... toward the water. I'll know when we're closer. Probably.&quot; She looks out at the sky again. &quot;Be ready to drive... defensively.&quot;<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T01:00:44-08:00","id":29194,"title":"","content":"<b>Cal</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The shock clears slowly, only to be replaced by truly deafening silence. No longer can you hear calculation and process, no longer do you know everything you need. instead...you notice more personal matters, matters you had never considered before. The palm of your right hand...you feel something hard and sharp digging into it, opening it - splaying fingers is an odd thing too really, all those bones and muscles, all moving under you volition, funny how you'd never considered <i>how</i> it does that - you find a thin sliver of metal from the damaged container, it drops from your palm to the floor leaving but a small red outline and a drop of blood. You'd never considered - wait, you'd never <i>considered</i> of your own volition at all - what an injury to a body <i>actually</i> meant. Oh academically sure you knew...but...it had never seemed anything more than a process, just one of many, plates shatter when dropped, cigarattes smoke triggers olfactory organs to fire messages to the brain, pointy things damage flesh.<br /> <br /> &quot;Tommy!? Tha fucks goin' on out there!?&quot;<br /> <br /> Your reverie breas as Reg's voice comes out from the building and you can hear the banging of footsteps as he moves through the building towards where you are.<br /> <br /> You know two things suddenly.<br /> <br /> 1. This is going to be hard to explain<br /> 2. You don't know where the other Angels in the city are anymore...</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Squid</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">You're making decent progress, taking the main route to the waterfront when you notice traffic slowing and building up all around. The traffic lights seem to be shifting to red all over. There's shouting and cursing from people and much frustrated horn blowing.<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm sorry Milady, we seem to have run into a traffic jam,&quot;<br /> <br /> He looks around at the road and cars around your vehicle, then pops out his phone and spends a few minutes checking something on it<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm not sure we'll be able to get out of here, according to this,&quot;<br /> <br /> He waves his phone in your direction<br /> <br /> &quot;There's gridlock all over Portsmouth and no one seems to have any idea why. I can't imagine anyone will be getting anywhere anytime soon.&quot;</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T19:01:35-08:00","id":29658,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">&quot;Inconvenient... I wish I could say unexpected. I'd hoped we could get somewhere before a response. The Machine governs its own, after all.&quot; She glowers at the traffic lights, then at the hood of the car. &quot;Even the Machines that are less burdensome to Gaia,&quot; she adds, maintaining the language of her cult as she talks about Edward's hybrid. She checks how far they are from the docks on her phone, considering walking, but really not wanting to for obvious reasons. &quot;There are times I wish I had wings,&quot; she mutters. &quot;Be watchful for an opening. We may need to leave quickly. We are not warriors.&quot; <i>And if something major did indeed happen by the docks, I'll be able to find out from some poor bastard later</i>, she muses to herself as she waits for the traffic to clear. She's grateful, not for the first time, that she's able to make sure she isn't wearing the nervousness she feels in this situation - it wouldn't do to shake her cultist's faith.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T22:49:52-08:00","id":29758,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The cleaning cart slid backwards with the weight Tommy was applying to stay upright and he fell back to the ground. The stones were slick with oil and other liquids, bringing to sharp relief the chaotic splintering and explosion of metal and melted plastics. Hearing Reggie in the distance, his first impulse was to stand back up but forgot which hand to lead with. The metal dug a little deeper and hit at raw nerve, the pain radiating everywhere robbing him of his voice for a moment and the footsteps drawing closer creating a momentary panic. Then he heard a different voice that elicited something else: anger.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"color:green\">&quot;This is just not your day, is it. Man can I relate. All I wanted was to breathe in that salty air and catch a sunrise hitting the water. Me and my associate. Guess we'll figure out some sort of arrangement though, right pal?&quot;</span></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Tommy cast his eyes about before realizing no one else was there. Yet anyway. But the damage had to be more severe than he could see to bring on auditory hallucinations. He tried to calm his senses and reach out, willing for a connection back to his handler. Hard as he tried though, it was like trying to jump an ignition with a dead battery. There was no response but worse than that was the feeling of losing where the lock, key and starter are at all.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"color:green\">&quot;Yeah, you're not phoning home pal. And you haven't lost your marbles. I hate to say that you're not going to be able to flit out of here---that would be ill-advised anyway. You should get out of dodge though, yes?&quot;</span></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> Tommy refused to just give way completely to the reality of the situation. He might not be able to call out but there had to be his toolbox to reach into. This proved to be an mistake and he recoiled inwardly at trying to touch what was there. The energies that he once relied on without thought and with a cleanness of flow now felt soiled and smudged, like the fumes of gasoline without the gas.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Finally he resigned himself to the foreign voice, &quot;You have sullied me. If you think that I'll let any of this stop me though from finishing my mission you are sorely mistaken. The package backed itself inside my memory and that is inviolable. There's at least 15 hours for me to get this to a drop-box. You failed.&quot;</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> A sharp laugh rang in Tommy's ears,<span style=\"color:green\">&quot;Go ahead and look at what they sent you here to do. But start multitasking because your hand will start to go cyanotic without proper medical attention and then we're both screwed.&quot;</span></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> Tommy conceded the point as the anger that had fueled him past the pain was giving way and he could feel the reality of that admonition. He dug through the cart and found a first aid kit stuck at the bottom on the left. After quick consideration, he decided against removing the splinter since there weren't any tools to stop a geyser should it be a major vein and settled on a firm wrapping of gauze.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">While doing this he cycled through the backed data uplink and found himself sick at the revelation, &quot;This is a trick. You're corrupting me more than I thought. There's no way this is right. There's nothing here.&quot;</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">For the first time there was no hint of malice. It seemed the voice was genuine in its pity, <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;Think about what you found and where you found it. Think about the information given to you before the undertaking. No specifics as to the contents or even a general notion. Unless the painting itself was the message. Or maybe you're not able to handle it. Maybe there is something there and you refuse to accept.</span></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">The painting! Tommy frantically felt for the framed Goya and pulled it free, this time mindful to use his left hand. He could hear Reggie getting closer but panting at the exertion of having tried to run the full distance. After grabbing a roll of duct tape, Tommy moved as quickly as he could to where the wrecking ball was stationed.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">He absently caught the name of the construction company as he slid to his knees and went to taping the painting to the underside of the machine, careful to not actually touch the painting itself but rather the brass studded frame.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> At this point, Reggie had caught a second wind and Tommy knew that he'd get to the crate at any minute. He looked down at the debris and picked up a jagged piece of metal. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;What are you thinking?&quot;</span> Tommy couldn't help but laugh as he thought, &quot;You don't know? I gotta sell this.&quot; He dragged the metal against his hairline above his left eye and the blood started to flow freely. At first there was silence and then, <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;Fine. Let me help you.&quot;</span></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">In his mind's eye, Tommy was seeing himself or rather he was approaching himself as the package began to be scanned. And then there was an impossible pain. He felt cleaved in two and then scattered. The passenger voice had Tommy live the moment of the passenger death.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">The sensation propelled him violently back to the crate and he slammed into it, slumping to the ground. He could taste the blood from the cut to his scalp and decided then on not to have any other bright ideas or goading fests.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Reginald Barnes didn't have words at first at the sight. He started to gag a little at the sight of the blood but managed to vocally be horrified too, &quot;I don't even---what am I---&quot;</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">The words came out in a rapid fire as he tried to simulate shock mentally, &quot;Reg! I was real careful with the lift and the crate. Hand to God but I guess it musta jostled a little when I set it down. There was this beeping noise and you know---I freaked out! I looked at the manifest and saw there was a car packed in with all this fancy stuff. I don't got no other job right now, you know you did a solid hirin me an all an I didn't want to get you in hot water. I undid the container and went to see if the car had started or somethin. They got these keyless ones and who knows right and it was a beaut and maybe I shouldn't have but I opened the door just to see cause ya know the battery coulda died and then this second beep started up. I saw these lights comin from the dash and damn it I shoulda left but ya just don't know with these electrics. There was somethin in there and a timer and I bugged the fuck out. I pushed my cart in I mean why would I push my cart in and then back out, ya know! and then I bolted it back shut or I thought I did but then whooshpow! Jesus Reg I don't feel good. I can't go to prison. I'm too pretty. Oh god my face. Tell me it ain't bad Reg.&quot;</div></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/257-calrabjohns","name":"Calrabjohns","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T02:36:20-08:00","id":29813,"title":"","content":"<b>Squid</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Minutes tick by, each one dull and frustrating. Casting your eyes around outside the windows of the car you see people going about their normal lives, shopping, walking, sitting and chatting. Well, except for those four. It's not much but something about that guys tattoo keeps drawing your eye. It's some vaguely abstract shape, just poking out from under the cuff of his shirt sleeve. The four of them look like white collar professionals out for a night of drinking, but they look quite serious and are making their way at a decent pace along the road toward the pier.<br /> <br /> The car's engine starts again, Edward had turned the engine off while you were sat in traffic.<br /> <br /> &quot;Milady, looks like we can start moving again, we'd have to turn off this main route though and take a chance on a side road or something if we want to get to the dock,&quot;</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Cal</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">&quot;Uh..um...uh...yo..you'll be...uh...fine! Yeah, fine. Uh. Just...let me go and...ambulance! Call one, err...just sit down for now or...uh...something. Don't move!&quot;<br /> <br /> Panicky he back away an pulls a phone out of his pocket cursing at it as he fumbles trying to turn it on - you notice that despite pressing the button the screen remains staunchly blank - until he curses loudly and dashes off to the building, perhaps trying to use the landline.<br /> <br /> There are murmurs all around as people - workers and otherwise from the dock - are gathering around talking and pointing, perhaps 20 in all. A guy rolling along a wheelie bin and picking up rubbish, a pair of gulls picking away at the detritus in his bin. A half dozen guys in a warehouse uniform from two buildings down, and morbidly curious onlooker in general. They seem content to watch - though a few seem to be going through the same troubles getting their phones to turn on, whether from trying to take photos or trying to call for help you can't be sure.<br /> <br /> A few gulls sitting across the edge of the roof of the building Reg went into are crying loudly. A dissonant dirge, strangely apt for the state you find yourself in.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T10:00:14-08:00","id":29968,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">(May as well try out some Compromise)<br /> &quot;Get there as soon as you're able... there's something that requires my attention.&quot; She smoothly opens the car door and leaves for the street, looking nonchalant as she moves in the same direction as the strange men and looks for an alley to duck into. (1 success on 3 stealth dice - whew)<br /> <br /> As soon as she finds one, she ducks out of sight and spends a few moments in concentration. If there were any observers, they would see subtle seams appearing in her skin and green, viny tendrils growing into her hair.<br /> (3 aether to activate swarm, mind reading, and sense the angelic - 2 successes on 10 dice on the compromise roll, rolling for glitch instead of condition - 2 successes on 3 dice (why can't the compromise roll have had that ratio!) so stick me with a transient Major glitch)<br /> <br /> Now, assured of her ability to scatter to the winds if spotted, she follows the men, keeping watch for angelic activity in the back of her mind while trying to get a read on the tattooed one. These four were just too suspicious to let pass - they had to be up to something.<br /> Not for the first time, she wishes she had more ravenously loyal lackies that she could just use to break some legs for her, rather than having to slink around on her own. Oh well - let the tree take root before trying to harvest the fruit. ...oooh, she'll have to use that one later.<br /> (1 success on 4 dice for mind reading)</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T12:52:57-08:00","id":30061,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Tommy affected a weak smile and slurred his words, his eyes seemingly lazed in their movements as he scanned the now very occupied pier, &quot;Shhur fing. I woen' moove.&quot; He waited for Reggie to clear half the distance between the crate and the building before snapping himself back to greater attention. The two people behind the guard rail that was in both sight and hearing range couldn't seem to get a signal and there were no snap-click sounds to indicate a picture being taken despite discernible effort for either of those things. He wanted to be completely sure though.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> Tommy slowly let himself slump down until he was partially obscured by the cleaning cart he'd manned earlier in the evening. As it was missing a good portion of the chassis, it wasn't hard to tip it over even with a casual graze with his left arm. It fell toward him and items fell out right and left. There were some gasps that he could hear and he could feel that at least one person was coming toward him to try and check on him. With the little time that he had, he ran his eyes over what was within reach. </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> The first aid kit had mercifully fallen against his stomach and a mop with wash cloth tangled on the handle was by his right foot. The luck ended there though. More useful items like the toolbox which he was fairly certain had valuable alcohol stowed away thanks to another worker, Lester, who applied the Eagle Scout philosophy of preparedness to getting shit-faced and then there was the cell phone he taped into the receptacle for emergencies---kind of like this.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">The phone he'd been carrying during the mission had definitively been destroyed after falling atop it at least four times over the course of as many hours. His right hand was throbbing and at the moment was crushed beneath his hip.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">He shook his legs until the mop was underneath one of them firmly with the other in place to do what was needed. There was no time though, unimpeded, as the Good Samaritan stood over him, concern etched on her face. </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">&quot;Sir, I think it'd be best if you let me wait with you. You're bleeding profusely and you really shouldn't be moving. Let me move that mop there. That could be dange--&quot;</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> Tommy was turning himself slowly to look up at this seemingly well-intentioned woman and to position the next action: he used the torque from a sharp twist of his knees to break the head off the mop and make it slightly more wieldy.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> The snapping sound of the mop didn't associate with the sound in that woman's mind though. She thought maybe a bone had popped and screamed, running toward the building to apprise Reggie of the new development.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">While a bone hadn't actually snapped, the twist did put undue pressure through Tommy's hip and into his arm. He made the most of the panic and laid on his stomach a moment, poking at the phone with the broken mop while cradling the aid kit to his stomach.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> Two of the workers idling by didn't feel comfortable in that role anymore and made their way toward Tommy. His face was wan and he was perspiring at fever rate. The splintered mop tore the tape and the phone dropped out of the bucket. He awkwardly swiped the mop at the phone and got it half-way to him before feeling a hand on his shoulder. </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">&quot;Yo guy, you really don't look so good. Ambulance should be here any minute so why don't we---&quot;</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> Tommy couldn't trust anything around him. He wheeled around with the mop and it smacked the man's shoulder. He recoiled and the friend took a step back too. Tommy edged backwards and palmed the phone in his busted hand, which was once more bleeding. The scalp had at least clotted but the previous flow had dried and did no favors to putting anyone at ease.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> &quot;Whoa there! Look, we don't want to hurt you but you're acting seriously messed up. I think that bleeding is screwin with your brain. Just---just try to relax.&quot;</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> Tommy pushed his feet on the ground until his back was pressed to the container. He used the mop to brace himself as he stood, barely holding the phone and kit with his busted hand. There was some truth to what the man said. Tommy had received a crash course on human sensation and limitation. He was feeling wobbly and nauseous. The only thing keeping him going was sheer paranoia.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">He walked with the makeshift cane and swung the aid kit in front of him. They backed off but were determined to do the right thing. &quot;My phone is busted but I'll head to the security station. Hit the alarm maybe or find a megaphone under the counter.&quot;</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> Tommy stumbled over the guard rail and people moved out of his way, shuffled toward a small alleyway that would soon lead into a tiny cobbled street with some houses and closer to a main road. He risked one last look to see if anyone was paying too much attention to his movements but there was no way to tell. The crazed gambit had paid out its last return. </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> Each step felt heavier but it was his hope that the space gained might have got him free of the suspected electronic interference. After rounding the corner, he fumbled at the phone and punched the first number on auto-dial. There was some sign of activity but the other end was scrambled. He couldn't be heard.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> &quot;Ok. Think dammit.&quot; He winced as he started to unwrap the gauze which had grown grimy and soaked in dry and fresh blood, awkwardly opening the kit to apply another thing of gauze and iodine which burned like napalm. He wrapped some along the cut on his head and pocketed the rest along with the iodine and laughably small scissors.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">No butterfly stitches or anything to keep the blood from really flowing. Couldn't use the aspirin because his blood won't clot. He tossed the rest away and went back to work on the phone but he'd stepped a little into the street and a car almost hit him. </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">&quot;What the fuck dude? Watch where---jesus you look like crap.&quot; Tommy limped until he could lean into the driver's door, &quot;Do you have a working phone?&quot; &quot;Well sure, I--that's weird. It was working just a second ago.&quot; &quot;Where.&quot; He motions behind him, &quot;I was on a call two blocks up by the church with the big stainglass tree up top. Are you gonna be able to--&quot;</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> Tommy let go of the window and walked without another word. The car drove off with no further incident. As he walked, the passenger finally spoke up, <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;Why are you bothering. You were planning to finish your mission right?&quot;</span> Maybe the passenger knew its host was fading because that exchange was like a shot of potent espresso, &quot;Yeah and I still might. But not if I'm dead. Don't get comfy though. I might not trust the mission right now but I definitely don't trust you.&quot; <span style=\"color:green\"> &quot;Fair enough. We're here.&quot;</span></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> There was an inviting tree and some soft looking grass that shared ground with the church. Tommy dropped to the ground and reveled in being still for a moment. The passenger resumed silence. If he weren't so tired, he would maybe think he was being managed but it didn't matter in that moment. He hit the third number on his speed dial, the one he didn't want to reach out to but he had no choice given where he might stand with the Marzinis thanks to Vinny. He was calling Yuri. </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">&quot;Yuri, it's Tommy. Don't hang up. I'm in the shit. Yeah---so much so I'm callin you. I need a pickup and a doctor. What do I have to give you? There's a Goya with your name on it but if you don't pick me up it's gone. I'm gone and the blood isn't that bad right? I'm in front of a church with a stainglass window. Giant tree in the glass and I'm under an actual tree. Please come.&quot;</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">He snapped the phone in half, took out the sim card and tossed the broken pieces as far as he could. His hands scraped at the dirt to bury the card but instead he gave in to shock and passed out. </div></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/257-calrabjohns","name":"Calrabjohns","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T02:01:04-08:00","id":30338,"title":"","content":"<b>Squid</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">[rolling vs stealth. Wits 2, Com 3, -2 dice as not really paying attention. 0 suxx. You're not noticed]<br /> <br /> You feel a slight mechanical clank and whirr, as though the gears on a car took a second longer to engage than planned and you notice with some aggravation that the veins and blood vessels on your left hand and up to about your elbow are now all fiercely visible. A thin tracery of blue and vague pinks, only visual but disconcerting none the less.<br /> <br /> Moving along behind the group - who are walking briskly and seemingly with purpose toward the docks - using what physical cover you can, from people to objects. Just quickly looking at them your ability to Sense the Angelic highlights the three untattooed as under some angelic affect, it seems to be guiding their actions subtly rather than any form of overt control.<br /> <br /> Your eyes then overlay as you try to scan through into the mind of the one that is not marked by the Angelic power.<br /> <br /> [rolling to resist Mind Reading, Resolve 2, 0 suxx]<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Gotta hurry, gotta get there in time. Find out if that's really a heretic. He'll - a sense of the angelic once again - reward me if it is,&quot;</i><br /> <br /> You get a sense of apprehension and avarice from them, as though they want this to be something real, something valuable to hand over.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Cal</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Sprawled out under the tree you lie in a state of semi-consciousness. Briefly cognizant of your immediate surrounding you notice four white collar men hurriedly making their way along the street toward the docks, followed shortly after by something screaming of god-machine influence, you twitch slightly, seemingly an uncontrolled response - from yourself or the <i>other</i> you are unsure - placing yourself just out of sight of the road.<br /> <br /> Again later you become briefly aware of talking and a chage in lighting above you but are unable to truly comprehend what it is, except that one of the voices sounds like Yuri. You feel pressure on your arms and a sudden shift of body position - your head lolling strengthlessly - followed by another sudden shift in body position as you are placed flat on something soft. The world fills with an engine rumble and you drift again to unconsciousness.<br /> <br /> [OOC: you're in the back of Yuri's car, he'll take you to somewhere safe, where that is is up to you as you know Yuri better than I do <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />]</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T19:09:15-08:00","id":30696,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">&quot;Take him to the doc-tore.&quot;<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">&quot;Isn't theeis the man who snaked those Etruscan vases from Yuri in Wales, a month back? Why are we 'elping him?&quot;</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">He could see Yuri, through flickering eyes, leaning from the front seat and looking down at him, a plume of smoke blown from a cigar down at his face, &quot;I am a humanitarian, Sergei. Man calls and tell me he is dying---I would have to be monster not to help him. Mr. Violet will take good care of him.&quot;</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">A silence fell over the car and strangely, Tommy felt himself deposited gently on the end of the limo directly behind the driver and Yuri. Sergei and the other muscle looked at Tommy as if he were an animal in a cramped cage at a shelter. That was the last thing Tommy saw before passing out in the car.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Tommy felt something cold against the tip of his nose. His vision was obscured as if the eyes were tearing up. Eventually he realized it was an acorn. He was back beneath the tree or maybe he had never left. He shifted his gaze to the right where he'd angled the toss of the phone and noticed a half of the broken device sticking up through the grass. So---the call was made.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">The sound of taps against the cobblestones returned his attention to the streets. He saw shined loafers and pressed slacks, metallic sunglasses and starched white collar shirts. Four dapper gentlemen running down the street and toward the alleyway he had made his way from. The image was so discordant he thought there might be music to follow. He was half-right.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"color:gray\">The universe is made up of several things, each playing and collaborating together in an exact way to make something work. Sound depends on harmonics. The turntable skips, the needle falls off and the wave breaks. Another time, Yesod.</span></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> An octocopter had lagged behind the four people. As they had rounded the corner, the copter hovered at the intersection and a camera rotated, dilated and it was clear that it saw Tommy. The blades buzzed and the copter bobbed as it leaned back and forth in its travel back to Tommy.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"color:green\"> &quot;Get up, Tommy.&quot;</span></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> The blades started to unfold and spindle legs touched the ground, a copter shifting into a spider. It skittered quickly but the gaps in the stone tripped it up some.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"color:green\">&quot;Get up Tommy.&quot;</span></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">The camera eye glowed a malignant red and the spider stuck two legs into the grass to stabilize. The back of the bloated body burst and thousands of little spiders started to crawl toward Tommy.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"color:green\">&quot;Get up!&quot;</span></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> Tommy woke up in a panic. He tried to raise his arms but a surge of pain followed. His legs were similarly immobilized. Wrists and ankles were manacled. Florescent lighting flickered and cast a sickly yellow glow from above him. He was in a small room covered wall to floor in plastic, the paint an ugly lime green.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">There were surgical instruments to the right of him and sitting on a pedestal in the corner of the room was a brown vase with a depiction of two Roman soldiers in an arena match. It was the Etruscan.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">&quot;I don't think our lot has improved considerably, IV.&quot; Tommy flexed his hand experimentally and was pleased at least to find that there wasn't a big thing of metal sticking out of it. The stitching was tender though and split some. He could feel an itchiness on his scalp where he'd made a cut. The metal was in a mason jar though and there was extensive writing on the label.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"color:green\">&quot;They took me into another room. I know that but I can't see anything. I'm still in your hoody pocket. Assuming IV means Inside Voice. That's rich but you can call me Jack. And we're better here than asleep. You were almost nabbed. Or I was.&quot;</span></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> There was some talking off in another room and the whirring of a oscillating fan. Otherwise the room was very quiet. &quot;I don't get it Jack. If the painting was the message, then I was pushed. That makes no sense to me. The blueprint was loaded with data. I can feel that. And then there's you---you did nothing. It was like you knew something. I'm flying blind here, Jack. Tell me one thing. One real thing.&quot;</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">No response. Not for a long time. A door opened and closed in the distance. Someone flipped through channels idly. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;It's a list, Tommy. You have a list. Detailed. There's two names left on it. Right below yours. That's all you get. I have every reason to lie though. And you won't get to read it. Not while I can help it. My turn. Are you going to try and make the drop?&quot;</span></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> His pulse quickened, breathing going sharp. Monitors started to beep with urgency. &quot;I have nine or ten hours left to decide that. If I'm even able. You're blocking whatever juice I'm supposed to have, aren't you.&quot; He didn't get a chance to hear Jack reply as a small man walked to the doorway and entered. He was in a white labcoat with a purple handkerchief and black leather apron. The plastic crinkled and squished as he walked in.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">&quot;It was my understanding that you know a little something about medicine, Mr. Facilli. I would think that you'd realize you shouldn't try and use your right hand with fresh stitches. Please don't mangle my work again. I take pride in my work.&quot; Mr. Violet sterilized a needle before reapplying the stitches. He then walked to the metal splinter. &quot;It's not very often I see this sort of metal, Mr. Facilli. And I can assure you that it would never be used in the construction of an automobile.&quot;</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> Tommy didn't say anything. He looked toward the open door and tried to make out how many rooms were in the facility he was in. The plastic sheeting hung over the door though in three strips and he couldn't see anything through the murky surface. This wasn't meant to be a conversation---not yet.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">&quot;Interesting day you've had, Mr. Vasilli. Yes, that's the name that went out on the radio for the incident at the pier. Quite a brouhaha. But why would they call you Vasilli and why wouldn't you let Yuri know. If he'd known you were a comrade, I'm certain your ministrations would be tendered by someone--disposed to tenderness.&quot;</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> Mr. Violet unscrewed the top of the mason jar and ran the splinter over his tongue. &quot;I can almost taste the Mover.&quot; Tommy almost choked. &quot;What the fuck are you talking about now?!&quot; Mr. Violet grinned and showed several teeth that looked like something you'd see in the mouth of a rapper. That was no gold or platinum lining his molars though.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">&quot;I wish you would show me the respect that is due me. After all, I've done you quite a few favors. The camera isn't on. Mr. Yuri Blagovich wanted you to beg for forgiveness for the Wales incident. Wanted me to detail how he got the vase, tracked down the diplomat from Iceland it wound up with and had me play Operation on the man. Blah blah blah.&quot;</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">He walked over to the vase and knocked it over. It shattered and pieces flew everywhere. The monitor sounded like a rapid telegraph. </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">&quot;The world is a strange place, Mr...hmm. I'm not sure which name you prefer. You've gone by Timothy and Tommy though. Let's call you, and please forgive me for this small indignity but, let's call you Mr. T. Mr. T, I think you and I have much more interesting things to discuss. This splinter, for one. We both know where it comes from. I have made it my business to collect this type of metal and make it a part of me. There is no greater honor than to become an instrument for The Mover. It's still so strange to speak of. I never believed that there was something that controlled the affairs of the world, behind the curtain. I didn't know there was a curtain. I was a man of science---I still am. But now I see the curtain. And it is glorious. Mr. T, that's not all I see. You are a very special bird.&quot;</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Mr. Violet injected something into a catheter sticking out of Tommy's arm. The effects were soporific. &quot;We wouldn't want you to have a cardiac arrest. There is much to do. But first, let's get some privacy. Yuri left some associates behind. It's a sad state of affairs when the trust is gone. Now, don't go anywhere.&quot;</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> The monitors calmed as the drug made its way through Tommy's veins. When Mr. Violet left, Tommy struggled at the bindings. &quot;I'm gonna die. God dammit.&quot; <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;For a fucking urn---what did you get me into.&quot;</span> Tommy wanted to kill Jack again but stayed those impulses. A piece of the urn had flown onto the surgical table near his left hand.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">He flexed his fingers desperately and managed to get the urn, twiddling it like a coin until it rested in his palm. He got a grip on it and began rubbing the jagged clay against the leather strap binding him. Panic was counteracting the narcotic. &quot;This is cutting me. I'll be handicapped by the dawn's morning light. Jack, you got to give me something or we're dead.&quot;</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> Sergei and another man entered the room. One walked over to the broken urn. &quot;You're really tryeeng to die, aren't you Tommy.&quot; Sergei shook his head, puzzled, &quot;He's bound up like I like my wimen: tight and ready to screw. This is odd. Violet turned kemra off. Yuri will kill that weasel.&quot; At that moment, Mr. Violet walked in. Sergei stepped into the doorway to bar an exit. </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> Mr. Violet smiled as he walked over to the man by the urn. &quot;You gentlemen have saved me a great deal of trouble. I was just planning to kill you both in horrifically painful ways.&quot; The man by the urn backhanded Mr. Violet, &quot;You are going to be fed to Sasha if I know Mr. Blagovich. Stupid lee-tle man.&quot; Mr. Violet slowly righted himself and then the air started to sizzle. It was shimmery like a mirage and then something more odd happened. The muscles underneath the apron and lab coat began to ripple until Mr. Violet looked like he could be a bodybuilder.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">He picked up the man who'd hit him with one hand and held him up with ease. The man's face started to turn purple and the hand holding him began to smell of burning flesh. And then he went alight. Sergei fumbled at his side for the gun in his pants. Tommy had managed to free one hand and cut at the other. </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"color:green\">&quot;Tommy, reach into your pocket and imagine a bottle of lighter fluid. Don't question it. Do it now.&quot;</span> Tommy didn't. He reached in and sure enough, it was there. Sergei hadn't managed to pull his piece yet. Tommy squeezed the lighter fluid as much as he could and the liquid arced to hit Mr. Violet who went completely alight.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">His screams pierced the air and he fell to the ground, rolling on the plastic lined floor. Tommy cut at the leather binding his feet and freed himself completely. Sergei stared disbelieving at the whole scene. &quot;Sergei, shoot him!&quot; He broke free of the reverie and got off a shot, hitting Mr. Violet in the leg. Tommy ran to the door and grabbed Sergei by the wrist. They both ran toward the end of the corridor.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Violet was still burning as he limped toward them. He threw skin that was sloughing off of his burning person. A piece hit Sergei in the back, who cried out. Tommy ignored everything but the metal hatch door. He threw Sergei bodily through the doorway which had fortuitously been left open.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Another glob of fatty tissue flew through the air. Tommy got on the other side and closed it just as Violet had bridged the gap. He twisted the metal wheel shut in time before it started to steam. Violet was pounding at the door. Tommy pulled Sergei up winding stairs until they were outside.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> Tommy recognized the black sedan as one that Sergei uses and ran to the passenger side door. Sergei went to the driver side and opened it for both of them. He started the car up and drove them both away.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">There was silence for a few minutes and then Sergei spoke with a cracked voice, &quot;What did I just see.&quot; Tommy turned to look at him, &quot;You think I know?? That freak was one of yours. What is wrong with you. And Yuri. I had a damn good thing lined up for him.&quot; He turned back around and stared ahead indignantly. He had to turn it around.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Sergei gripped the steering wheel until his knuckles went white, &quot;I would say sorry but I just saw friend burned alive by some Frankenfucker. Cameras were rolling in every room in there except what Violet turned off. They're transmitting to remote location. Yuri will know what happened and I will vouch for anything he couldn't see. You seved my life.&quot;</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> Tommy noticed that they had driven by Daisy Antiques. He waited until they were three blocks further until he spoke, &quot;You can let me out here.&quot; Sergei stopped the car, &quot;Tommy, this isn't free pass. If you cross Yuri, I will do what I must.&quot; He unlocked the door and Tommy exited the car.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">&quot;Yuri is a lucky man then. Do me one more favor though. If Violet isn't six feet under, let me know.&quot; Sergei looked at Tommy incredulously, &quot;You really think---nevermind. I don't want to know. Call my number when you hev new phone and I'll store. I'll tell.&quot; He drove off without another word.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> The walk to Daisy Antiques was slow. Tommy stuffed his hands into his pockets experimentally but found he couldn't tap that energy. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;If you try to do that anymore, you might tear a hole. You were lucky that it worked as well as it did. And that they didn't bother patting you down. I can't believe we're still vertical.&quot;</span></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">&quot;Yeah. But if you keep inhibiting me, that could all change. We need to work together. Look, there's eight or nine hours before that drop point is decommissioned. I'll give you seven to convince me to stay.&quot;</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"color:green\">&quot;Who are you kidding, Tommy. You're still thinking about your cut of the painting. That whole business with being square with Yuri, the haggling with Vinny even before you meet with that Marzini guy, going to Daisy. You have a life that you want. I don't need to tell you anything about that list. But I will do this---I'll help you take the training wheels off. Because that Violet saw me and he sounded like he's seen everything plenty of times. This is an unusual circumstance and I can say with certainty he's not dead yet.&quot;</span></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> Tommy stopped three stores away from Daisy Antiques, &quot;How do you know that.&quot;</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"color:green\"> &quot;He found the eyes. I can't say more. The vestiges of my consciousness have been incorporated into you. We're joined at the hip now. But this is still not good.&quot;</span></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> Tommy stood at the doorway and knocked, &quot;Yeah, I didn't think it would be. There's probably a safety station in there for him to rinse off. Making friends everywhere. But this place---we're good here.&quot; He spoke again with the knock, &quot;Gaines, lemme in bud. Please.&quot; The drugs that had been coursing through his body overcame him now that he was out of danger's way.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">[OOC: I'm sorry but once I started writing---it just came out. Safety is a relative term. That was safer than getting captured by the GM or an agent. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />]</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">[OOC: I did roll for In My Pocket for the lighter fluid (Dex+Larc) and got a natural 10. 2, 6, 10, 2, 2 to be exact. There's been times when I thought I should roll but I didn't know how to do it. With that first scene, when Tommy was going to deceive Reggie about the fall, I thought of rolling Manip.+Subterfuge versus Reggie Wits+Composure with either a positive modifier for Tommy making another cut or a negative for Reggie to represent freaking out. It's not out of a lack of desire for strictures. I'm just not sure how to do contested rolls and other things. I have a vague idea of what I would do in retrospect but it's all pretty new to me. If I'm a problem, let me know please. I want to be a good player.]</div></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/257-calrabjohns","name":"Calrabjohns","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T19:44:28-08:00","id":31426,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Well. Whoever these men were, they were certainly up to no good. And in a hurry.<br /> <br /> A thuggish Destroyer might drop down in the middle of them, rough them up and drive them off. No. She was nothing like that rusting monstrosity. She'd make the institutions that kept the gears turning turn against these patsies of the Machine.<br /> <br /> She drops back enough to be out of earshot and dials 999 on her cellphone. &quot;Help!&quot; she whispers as soon as the operator picks up, affecting a frantic tone. &quot;There are some men heading toward the docks, they're dressed up like they're supposed to be respectable people but one of them has <i>tattoos</i>! And they're talking about <i>heretics</i>! I think they might try to blow something up!&quot; She seems completely earnest, as demons always do, as she takes a stroll through all the 'terrorist' stereotypes she can bombard the emergency operator with, and then go on about how they're recruiting homegrown ones for good measure. With any luck, she'll have the police whipped up into a frenzy aimed at the tattooed man she describes, and she gives a detailed location and direction of travel to make sure they know where to go.<br /> (3 manip + 2 persuasion: 8,4,5,1,(10, 9) - 3 successes)<br /> <br /> Just to ice the cake, and make this apparently mostly-willing pawn of the Machine's life hell for a night, she focuses on his description in her mind, and then jerks her head to the side a bit as if tugging at a loose thread of reality with her teeth. She envisions whatever legitimate business he might have to be here, whatever legitimate cover he might have... lost, like that loose thread in the wind.<br /> (3 manip + 3 subterfuge - unknown target's composure for Unperson, will let ST roll)<br /> <br /> She keeps on following them for now, creeping along behind, staying just barely close enough to keep them in sight as they keep going toward the docks. (will make another stealth roll if asked)</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T10:31:58-08:00","id":31764,"title":"","content":"<b>Cal</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">&quot;Who is it?&quot;<br /> <br /> Gaines' voice comes through the door, as footsteps approach it. There's a slight shake to the door as though a hand were placed on the handle but no sign that it was opening.<br /> <br /> Street lights light the street and the few passers-by briefly stare at you as you prop yourself up against the doorway, A council worker empties a rubbish bin. The night is far from silent, cars rush past and a pair of seagulls caw at one another from across the street.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Squid</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">&quot;Mam, please keep calm. These people, can you answer some questions...&quot;<br /> <br /> There is a back and forth and you get the feeling that the officer on the end of th eline is coming round to believing you after several minutes of discussion.<br /> <br /> &quot;Ok, I have sent Dispatch officers to the scene and supporting teams are on the way. Can I ask that you make your way to the nearest police station shortly to take your evidence and a statement,&quot;<br /> <br /> While phrased as a request you know it was anything but.<br /> <br /> [Man 3 + Sub 3 - Com 3 = 3 dice. 1 suxx]<br /> <br /> The four continue hurrying until three of them turn upon the fourth and seem to close ranks around them, looking hostile, they begin to argue, the tattooed man's body language screams incredulity until one of the three pushes him away and sends him sprawling to the floor. The three then turn away and continue hurrying to the docks. The tattooed fourth man sits on the pavement - confused surprise spread across his features - sitting half upright, hands behind him having broken the fall.<br /> <br /> Onlookers walk around him, not ignoring him outright, but as though with disdain.<br /> <br /> Walking past you make your way to the docks.<br /> <br /> It doesn't take long to establish where the excitement is. A large shipping container has seemingly exploded and sent semi melted metal fragments across the docks, the large crane used to unload it has had the glass shattered and flash burns across one side. A lone ambulance - lights flashing - sits nearby, surrounded by a large crowd of onlookers, a fat, balding middle aged man is gesturing and speaking loudly to a paramedic, standing right beside the shipping container.<br /> <br /> In the distance the sound of sirens can be heard, with the traffic as bad as it is likely moving very slowly.<br /> <br /> The three remaining agents have spread themselves through the crowd, you retain sight of only one, who is garrulous and invitingly speaking with the bystanders.<br /> <br /> Most chillingly your senses scream of the God-Machine but no one thing draws your attention fully, as though this is a place where the God-Machine's interest has been recently but nothing more.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T16:53:55-08:00","id":32832,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">&quot;Serves him right,&quot; she murmurs to herself.<br /> <br /> With all the people around, Greene decides it's finally time to make full use of the advantages she called forth and slips behind some of the dockside clutter. A few moments later, a thin carpet of beetles, crickets, centipedes, and all other sort of woodland creepy crawlies with a faint metallic sheen winds its way out, sticking to the shadows and thinning out to avoid being noticed as more than a background nuisance. Hmm. Baldy, hysteric and feeling confident enough to harangue the paramedic, probably saw something, or at least is in charge here... She positions herself to get a good view of the patient being loaded into the ambulance, or rather a thousand good views, and a thousand copper eyes focus in and go fishing.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">OOC info: (Aether point spent; Wits + Subterfuge - assumed Resolve of 2:<br /> 2013-12-18 17:52:28 Ms. Greene rolls 3 dice to mind reading 9,4,8 (2 successes))</div></div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T16:16:39-08:00","id":33504,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Tommy held his left hand over the right forearm as he realized the catheter tube was still attached. He wasn't privy or acclimated to how often and what times workers toil to ferry and dispose of trash; however, he was confident that seeing them nearly everywhere he turned was an unusual display of civic pride and dedication. &quot;Sir, I am so embarrassed to admit this but I mistook your establishment for a flower shop. That'll teach me to read the whole sign. I'm here for a pickup. The Facilli wedding.&quot;<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Mr. Gaines took his hand off the handle, &quot;That's understandable young man. There's a shop with the same address number but different street. It's quite far though. If you'd like, I can call you a cab or--,&quot;. Tommy interjected, looking idly at one of the gulls, &quot;Actually, I could use a gift to bring along too. Maybe you could let me buy something? I know it's late but it would be greatly appreciated.&quot; &quot;I suppose I could, young man. Would you mind coming round back though. The phone is there and I'd rather not open the front, after business hours.&quot;</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> Tommy tapped the door two times and dashed off a thank you before walking down the steps and going round the corner ready to go through the back which in and of itself had a nice garden. He knew it would take Gaines a few minutes to maneuver through the storefront and get to the back where his living quarters were. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;You might want to reconsider this stop off.&quot;</span></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> Tommy walked up the rear stairs and sat in a little bench on the porch. He ignored Jack's warning and waited until Gaines opened the door. Gaines took tentative steps toward the opening, using a cane to help his steps. He reached out with a wrinkled hand and lightly brushed at Tommy's shoulder.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">&quot;Come in quick, boyo. You can tell me what is happening inside.&quot; Tommy didn't need to be asked twice. He stepped in and sat down at the tiny table in the kitchen while Gaines did the padlocks and chains. Rhythmic taps as Gaines walked his wood floor with taps on his slippers and a tap from his cane.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">He gripped the back of the chair Tommy was sitting in, then onto his shoulder, &quot;What in blazes have you got into this time, boy.&quot; One more squeeze before Gaines walked over to the stove, &quot;I was about to make some hot chocolate before turning in. Sure you'll say no like usual but---&quot;</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">As if on cue, Tommy's stomach grumbled and he realized that he'd be hungry from now on, &quot;Actually that sounds great Kingsley. Would it be trouble to have a sandwich too?&quot; Kingsley Gaines laughed as he rummaged through the fridge, pulling out some provolone, salami and whole milk, &quot;I don't think I've ever heard anything remotely like that come from your stomach. Are you really the Daniel I know?&quot;</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> Tommy let the question go by quietly. He pulled a rag hanging from a bar in the kitchen and tied it where the catheter was, tossing the tubing into a nearby trash can. &quot;It's not a social call unfortunately. That bag I left here, clothes and phone. I need it. An hour or ninety minutes tops to get straightened up.&quot;</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Three ticks before the pilot light took and the milk was set on the stove with three bits of chocolate melting in, &quot;You don't have to ask for that,&quot; he said with the chiding one might get from a family member. </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> Tommy pulled the rag tight before resting his hands on the table, leaning back in the chair and sighing loud, &quot;I know, Kingsley. It's just been a very, very long night and it's not over. I need the van too. Key'll be in the wheelwell. I'll let Parker know in the morning.&quot; Kingsley reached up to the cabinet and pulled out some rye bread and a skillet. Butter from the fridge and a spatula. &quot;What happened tonight, Daniel.&quot;</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> Tommy sighed, &quot;It's Tommy, Kingsley. And I---tripped.&quot; The bread sizzled a little as it was pressed into the pan with cheese and meat on top, &quot;That's what I said. Don't pull my leg. You're still messing around with those hooligans. Maybe I should have turned you in when you broke into the shop. You certainly haven't changed your ways.&quot;</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> Tommy stood up and went into a different cabinet, pulling out mugs and plates. His hand brushed a picture taped to a gaudy yellow cup. It was of Kingsley and his son Daniel. They were both laughing or something. Tommy had never asked about what. He didn't want to.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">&quot;I've got something lined up. One good thing to happen tonight. A Goya over at Fredericks Construction.&quot; He put the plates and mugs on the counter where Kingsley almost scalded him with food and drink alike. He sat back down knowing this was not what Kingsley wanted to hear. </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">&quot;Unless Fredericks has decided to expand, I am very surprised to hear this. He doesn't know from paintings to beans if you asked him who Goya was. This has to do with that business on the pier, doesn't it.&quot; The plate clattered as it met the table and a bit of grease hit Tommy on the cheek. Kingsley placed the mugs and slowly sat down across from Tommy.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> To assuage hunger and take shelter from the probing, Tommy took a sip from the hot chocolate. He winced as it burned some even as he let out a contented sigh at the first thing he'd really eaten. Kingsley sighed and reached a trembling hand to grasp at Tommy's hand, &quot;I just don't want you to get hurt, Da--Tommy. You just remind me of him.&quot;</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> Tommy leaned back until their hands weren't in contact, &quot;Yes. It does. If you need me to go, I understand. I don't have what we agreed on to partner up and these are dangerous people. Just let me clean up and I won't bother you again.&quot;</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">He retreated into the grilled cheese and salami sandwich, the blood loss and drugs making him hungrier than he otherwise would be and nausea was creeping in. The whole situation made him uncomfortable. It was easy to turn off the old man's stories and kindnesses when he could tune in to another channel and update a detail for a transaction with Yuri or John.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> Kingsley was only a little absentminded. He stood up too fast and his balance was a little off. Tommy made to help him but Kingsley waved him away. He gripped his cane and claimed his mug, turning sharply or as sharp as he could to make his way to the stairs, </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">&quot;You're not getting away that easily, Mr. Facilli. You broke a window and had Svensborg clock pieces in that rucksack when I caught you. You have a debt. I can't seem to get you to work it off honestly. Do what you have to tonight and then get that painting. At your commission for sales of purloined treasures, that should give you a quarter of what you owe me. I trust you'll lock up when you leave. Bag is in the closet behind the towels. Good night, Daniel.&quot;</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> Tommy almost said something but the last word made him quiet. He returned to his meal, then washed the dishes, made his way up the stairs and retrieved the bag with fresh clothes, a little walking money, basic picks, knife and phone.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">He zipped the bag over his hand so the stitches wouldn't get soaked as he showered. The dried blood flaked away and went down the drain. He almost forgot the next step as the hot water came down and then Jack spoke up, <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;How long were you down here? You've got more than a few people who know you. Very odd arrangement.&quot;</span></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> Tommy leaned against the tiles and let the water drip, &quot;The crate was delayed. Before that, I just kept building. Stealing. Kingsley caught me one night, as I'm sure you figured out. The full gaze of my handler was on me as Kingsley walked that slow walk with those tap slippers---I made those because he'd miss a step and I had to keep lending my shoulder to help him ambulate about the store. It was a pain. He doesn't fall anymore really now that he waits for those clicks. Where was--right, the full weight.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">It was like walking the surface of a high gravity asteroid, bones crunched and veins popped. Kingsley sat me on the couch and dabbed my head with a washcloth. He thought I was having some sort of panic attack and said we could work it out. My cover was saved, stronger than ever actually. I split my time between painting fakes and fixing up broken sundries for the shop and the janitor thing too. It was perfect.&quot;</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> Tommy dried off and brushed his teeth. <span style=\"color:green\">&quot;Sounds like you were due for ground patrol any day. An Escher angel, looped tumbler. Just be glad your pasta loving friends haven't picked up the slack.&quot;</span></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> Tommy unzipped the bag and put on the black jeans, white shirt and gray track jacket hastily with a set of sneakers. He stuffed the various items from the bag in pockets and left without further delay through the back. Key in the wheelwell, turn the ignition and peel out from the alleyway to Fredericks Construction. With almost perfect detachment, &quot;You're probably right.&quot;</div></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/257-calrabjohns","name":"Calrabjohns","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T11:30:55-08:00","id":34524,"title":"","content":"<b>Squid</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">From your new...perspectives...you find that the paramedics have clearly been here for a while - meaning these were called out well in advance of your call to the police - and they aren't loading anyone into the ambulance. In fact, your scanning of the man's minds expresses confusion and panic.<br /> <br /> There was a worker - worked for the balding man - called Tommy. He was unloading expensive art from the shipping container and Reggie, the owner of the shipping company, was inside doing general paperwork. Something crazy happened, Reggie heard noise and saw a bright flash and hurried his way to the loading bay. Once he arrived the container had been destroyed - melted and exploded - and Tommy was bleeding from the head and stumbling about like a man severely concussed. No one could get their mobile phones to work so, leaving Tommy with the instruction to stay where he was Reggie went inside and used the landline to call in the ambulance for the emergency.<br /> <br /> When Reggie came back outside and the ambulance arrived Tommy had gone missing entirely.<br /> <br /> And...hmmm...what's that under the crane?</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Cal</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">It's late night at this point, traffic cleared - according to the radio there had been complete traffic chaos earlier today - and, then, confusingly, a story on the news about a terror incident on the docks and a missing person. Seems someone had called the police and other emergency services and fed them some line about terrorism.<br /> <br /> In fact...your journey seems quite quick and devoid of any hindrance, not even a traffic light to interfere.<br /> <br /> [please roll wits+composure and include any bonuses from any abilities for spotting/noticing things]</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T18:14:31-08:00","id":34695,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Tommy tapped away on his phone with one hand while driving with the other. He was running searches on the construction site itself, information that a contractor would want to know such as how many models of a certain machine there would be for rent and the manner in which they're kept up.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">After scrolling through the filler of smiling faces and people standing over a desk staring intently at a blueprint, he found a few photos and text that were what he was looking for. </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">One of them was an exterior overhead shot of the construction yard that showed a few machines outside on the lot. The cranes were situated outside of the general warehouse because of the height differential and for safety purposes. There were six out there along with precut girders at any one time for a given job and lifts to move them as well. Two big wheeler trucks flanking each side of the warehouse.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">The fences were about 2.14 meters in height with razor wire up top and 186 square meters across with a half meter brick lining the ground immediately behind the fencing. Keypad with speaker for incoming vehicles and swipe card readers for employees.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"color:green\">&quot;You don't find it a little peculiar that we've hit no lights and have not seen a single car? Keep your attention more on the road.&quot;</span></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> Tommy turned on the radio in time to hear two newscasters segue from the end of one pier misadventure in the evening to weather, &quot;Well I was ready to think we had a small stroke of luck but no---I would have to agree now that things are odd.&quot;</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">He parked the van to the east of the yard where he was fairly certain the crane he was looking for was parked and tried to break in through a service entrance into the warehouse.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">The specs for building security weren't updated in the less public information venues though. Instead, Tommy heard the pullback on a shotgun from a security guard he had no notion was there. He raised his hands very, very slowly.</div>[So---I rolled six die over at Invisible Castle but that was days ago. I'm still locked out from using it. Maybe from keeping the window open when I was writing up the post. I used Squid's die roller and got a DF, which has been a day or two ago I think. Between the two sites, in order, they were 1 Except. Success, 1 regular and DF. I edited with using the previous successes for initial set-up and DF for the ultimate lapse.] <a href=\"http://www.umbralechoes.com/WoD2Roller.php\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.umbralechoes.com/WoD2Roller.php</a></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":257,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/257-calrabjohns","user":"Calrabjohns","date":". 12-26-2013, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/257-calrabjohns","name":"Calrabjohns","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T11:28:40-08:00","id":35025,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The spread cloud of insects rubs all its wings in irritation at apparently being too late. Oh well, then at least the agents of the Machine must have been, too. The eyes try to keep digging, searching for details of this Tommy's face in the man's memory, boring down until they find what they're looking for.<br /> (1 more succ for mind reading)<br /> <br /> Once satisfied, the swarm scuttles back into shadow to wind its way toward the crane and the glimpse of something unusual beneath it.<br /> <br /> In the back of the hive mind, it wonders if its cultist has managed to get close to the docks yet.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T10:37:03-08:00","id":38337,"title":"","content":"<b>Cal</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">[ooc: no guns, this is the UK. Especially on a security guard, they won't even carry a truncheon, it would be a guy with a radio and a big, sturdy flashlight]<br /> <br /> The man - late 30s or early 40s, of Nepalese descent - removes his hand from your shoulder as you turn to face him, he keeps the flashlight on, pointed at your face.<br /> <br /> &quot;Who are you and what are you doing here at this time?&quot;<br /> <br /> He moves confidently on his feet, and seems to exude an aura of controlled, calm, physicality.<br /> <br /> The only sounds are the dull rumble of the occasional car and some forlorn whistling from inside.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Squid</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Cal will give you the description of what Reggie knows about Tommy.<br /> <br /> The painting looks like this<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.franciscodegoya.net/All-Will-Fall-large.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.franciscodegoya.net/All-Will-Fall-large.html</a></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","user":"Scutarii","date":".  Added to Squid's section. 12-29-2013, 11:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T21:31:48-08:00","id":38577,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">[ooc: Forgot about that. I just didn't want to take it easy on Tommy for a DF. I'll remember now short of criminals and police.]</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Tommy shields his eyes reflexively from the glare of the flashlight by a raise of one hand. Once adjusted, he lowers it slowly and looks off to the side affecting abashment, &quot;This is so stupid. I came around to get Jerome's wallet. He told me he'd forgotten it or that's what I remember anyway. You know Jerome, right? He's one of the crew from Fredericks that's on the pier job tearing down some of the adjacent buildings for expansion or somethin.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> Well, I was down there earlier in the evening when that huge explosion happened and I really need a pint somethin fierce. Shit scared me half to death. I'm just not thinking straight man. Should of checked in the front.&quot;</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">He hooked his thumbs into his jean pockets, pulling them with what he hoped seemed anxious energy but always aware that one of those thumbs was brushing against the switchblade he'd taken from the bag at Daisy Antiques. If he had to, he could pull it out. Not without getting a solid knock from this guy though and he wasn't confident of prevailing without need for another medical service. &quot;You understand, right man? It's just been a messed up day.&quot;</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">[I rolled Manp.+Subterfuge for an attempted lie. If there's any penalties that should be applied, just let me know in the next post I guess.]</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><a href=\"http://invisiblecastle.com/roller/view/4345837/\" target=\"_blank\">5d10=30</a></div></div></div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Reginald Barnes, called Reggie by Tommy and anyone else willing to try to be friendly with the guy when he's not taking on airs. He lost his shit though during the brouhaha on the docks and talks no differently than anyone else that works in the pier when danger struck.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">[Thoughts]: &quot;Tommy, or should I say Timothy? A loudmouthed, overly familiar, slick hooligan. He's always primping in front of the mirror in his locker, combed back black hair and trying to hide his lack of style with just simple clothing, black jeans and white button shirt. Acted like he was being imposed on to wear those boots and orange vest over that grey sweatshirt for work. Short man with weasely looking features. Loud.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">I fell for his song and dance about needing a job to start fresh. And look what he does. He goes and blows up a crate! What else should I think with him running from the scene? I'm stuck here with a record for a Timothy Vasilli even though I've heard his friends call him Tommy. Ruffians too. Act like they're in the mafia. God maybe they are.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">I need to doublecheck everything on record. That PO box is certainly real. Checks are cashed regularly. I never needed to know anything else but god I might be in real trouble. That home address is probably fake. Wait. Where did he make me go drinking that one time. The Dog's Paw? Lion's Den? Something with an animal. I bet he goes there all the time. He has to.&quot;</div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/257-calrabjohns","name":"Calrabjohns","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T17:19:48-08:00","id":38981,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ms. Greene takes note of all that as she listens in on the man's mind, making special note to cross reference nearby pubs with appropriately-themed animal names. She keeps digging, trying to find his password for his office computer. Once that's accomplished, or not, her swarm starts crawling under the crane to take a good look at the painting lost under the crane, not just the image but any irregularities of the canvas or framing itself.<br /> <br /> (not entirely sure what I should roll for all of that, will leave it to the ST)<br /> <br /> Once she finds anything, or not, she starts buzzing off to the harbor office to try and find this &quot;Tommy's&quot; records.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T05:20:43-08:00","id":41650,"title":"","content":"<b>Cal</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">OOC: No guns for the police either, it's the UK! The only people with guns you might actually meet are criminals. Also, you're a Demon, he can't tell if you're lying unless you want him to know you're lying!<br /> <br /> &quot;Hmmm. No. I've been working here for a few years, there's no one I know of called Jerome and even if there were they'd know no one is allowed on site after it's closed. Let me lead you out,&quot;<br /> <br /> He gestures with his left hand (right is holding the torch at shoulder level), non-threatening but his body language reads as a firm order to go where he points you.<br /> <br /> You notice he's not leading the way but making sure that you'd in front of him...</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Squid</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">OOC: A crazy roll of Wits+Investigate gives you <b>8</b> successes! Int+Academics to know/recognise about the painting itself however turns up 0.<br /> <br /> The painting itself looks to be the real deal, oil work, canvas, slightly faded by the light. The frame seems newish though, as if someone had given it a new one a few month ago or something. It's clearly been taken and stashed here under the crane, wedged in such a position that it wont fall free and won't get damaged by the wheels - though perhaps some of the crane mechanism itself may damage it. Brushing your fingers against the painting itself gives you a brief flash - like someone flashing a strobe light into your eyes first thing in the morning - the fading remnants of your Sense for the God-Machine tells you that this is important somehow...</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}